{"id":39,"word":"Blurb","category":"Entertainment & Leisure","subcategory":"Books & Reading","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"બ્લૅર્બ","english_meaning":"A short promotional description of a book on its back cover or in a catalogue.","gujarati_meaning":"પુસ્તકના પાછળના કવર અથવા સૂચિ-ગ્રંથ પર ટૂંકો પ્રમોશનલ વિવરણ.","synonyms":["book description","synopsis","jacket copy"],"antonyms":["review","full summary"],"collocations":["back-cover blurb","write a blurb","book blurb"],"word_forms":["blurbs"],"usage_note":"Term coined by Gelett Burgess in 1907. A good blurb entices readers without spoiling the plot.","memory_tip":"'blurb' = ટૂ-ઉ-ટ-વ → blurb = પુસ્તક-ઢ-ટ.","examples":["The blurb sounded exciting, so she bought it.","He wrote the blurb for his friend's novel.","A catchy blurb can boost book sales.","She judged the book by its blurb."]},
{"id":40,"word":"Protagonist","category":"Entertainment & Leisure","subcategory":"Books & Reading","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"પ્રૉટૅગ્ૉ'નિસ્ટ","english_meaning":"The main character in a story or play.","gujarati_meaning":"વાર્તા અથવા નાટકનો મુખ્ય પાત્ર.","synonyms":["main character","hero","central figure","lead"],"antonyms":["antagonist","villain","minor character"],"collocations":["story protagonist","protagonist's journey","complex protagonist"],"word_forms":["protagonists"],"usage_note":"The antagonist opposes the protagonist. A flawed protagonist is a compelling narrative device.","memory_tip":"'proto' = ગ્રીક 'first' = પ્રથમ + 'agonist' = actor → protagonist = મુખ્ય-પાત્ર.","examples":["The protagonist overcomes many challenges.","She identified with the novel's protagonist.","The protagonist's growth drives the story.","A compelling protagonist keeps readers hooked."]},
{"id":41,"word":"Epilogue","category":"Entertainment & Leisure","subcategory":"Books & Reading","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ઍ'પિલૉગ","english_meaning":"A section at the end of a book or play that comments on or provides a conclusion to what happened.","gujarati_meaning":"પુસ્તક અથવા નાટકના અંતે એ ભાગ જે ઘટનાઓ ઉપર ટિપ્પણ અથવા નિષ્કર્ષ આપે.","synonyms":["afterword","conclusion","postscript"],"antonyms":["prologue","introduction","preface"],"collocations":["book epilogue","brief epilogue","written epilogue"],"word_forms":["epilogues"],"usage_note":"Opposite of prologue (introduction). An afterword is similar but more informational.","memory_tip":"'epi' = ગ્રીક 'after' = પછી + 'logue' = શબ્દ → epilogue = ઉ-ત-ભ-ભ.","examples":["The epilogue revealed what happened years later.","She read the epilogue to find closure.","The author added an epilogue to the revised edition.","The epilogue tied all the loose ends."]},
{"id":42,"word":"Prologue","category":"Entertainment & Leisure","subcategory":"Books & Reading","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"પ્રૉ'લૉગ","english_meaning":"An introductory section of a book or play that provides background information.","gujarati_meaning":"પુસ્તક અથવા નાટકનો પ્રાસ્તાવિક ભાગ, જે પૃષ્ઠભૂ-માહિતી આપે છે.","synonyms":["introduction","foreword","preface","opening"],"antonyms":["epilogue","conclusion","ending"],"collocations":["story prologue","dramatic prologue","prologue to the novel"],"word_forms":["prologues"],"usage_note":"A foreword is written by someone other than the author; a prologue is part of the story itself.","memory_tip":"'pro' = ગ્રીક 'before' = પહેલા + 'logue' = શબ્દ → prologue = પ-ઉ-ઉ.","examples":["The prologue set the scene beautifully.","He skipped the prologue and started chapter one.","The prologue hinted at the story's themes.","A well-written prologue draws readers in."]},
{"id":43,"word":"Footnote","category":"Entertainment & Leisure","subcategory":"Books & Reading","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ફૂ'ટ-નૉ'ટ","english_meaning":"A note printed at the bottom of a page, giving extra information about something in the main text.","gujarati_meaning":"પૃષ્ઠના નીચે ભાગ પ્રિન્ટ થઈ, મુખ્ય ટૅક્સ્ટ-ની-વસ્તુ-વિશે-વધારાની-માહિતી આપતી નોંધ.","synonyms":["endnote","annotation","marginal note"],"antonyms":["main text","body text"],"collocations":["add a footnote","see footnote","scholarly footnote"],"word_forms":["footnotes","footnoted"],"usage_note":"Footnotes appear at the bottom of the page; endnotes appear at the end of the chapter or book.","memory_tip":"'foot' = પૃષ્ઠ-ના-નીચે + 'note' = નોંધ → footnote = નીચે-ટ-ટ.","examples":["The academic text was full of footnotes.","She added a footnote to clarify the term.","Footnotes provide extra context.","The footnotes were longer than the text itself."]},
